// Serialising a handle is meaningless: whatever is written out cannot decode back to the same
// mutable object, because what makes it mutable is an index into a native table belonging to one
// thread. So the derives refuse it by name.
//
// They used to fail *incidentally*, with "call to undefined function 'mutable_array_to_json' -- ...
// or write 'mutable_array_to_json' by hand and import it with 'use'" -- an invitation to do the one
// thing that cannot work. Writing that function would have made the derive succeed and produce
// nonsense.
//
// Nested on purpose: the field is an `Option<MutableMap<...>>`, which a field-level check would miss
// and the recursive one catches.
#[derive(Json)]
struct Holder {
    slot: Option<MutableMap<string, int>>
}

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
